WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:00.973
- Hi, Drew.

00:00:00.973 --> 00:00:03.580
I heard that you liked my DIY TV frame,

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.940
and so here are my
step-by-step instructions

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.550
on how to do it.

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:11.310
You buy baseboard molding
and then cut it at 45 degrees

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:15.350
to the size of your TV and
spray paint the pieces.

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:18.890
You get wood appliques and
spray paint those as well.

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:22.350
Put your frame together
and add corner braces.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:24.090
Add hanging hardware.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:27.470
And I decided to add this
step of more definition

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:29.293
by adding crown molding trim.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.840
I cut those at 45 degrees,

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:35.560
added them onto the inside of my frame,

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.810
and I then just spray
painted that as well.

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:40.160
I added an extra step
of putting Rub 'n Buff

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:42.910
for the antique gold finished look.

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:46.740
Here's where I mount the frame,
put the TV on the TV mount,

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:50.070
and the final step is
adding some gold washi tape

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:51.870
around the edge of the frame.

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:54.790
This way, you get rid of the
black frame around your TV

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:56.800
and your remote sensor will still work,

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.363
and it blends seamlessly
with your new gold frame.

